---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/DesignArrow.astro';
import AuditClose from '../components/AuditClose.astro';
---
<Site description="Compare the free Growth Review, $750 Website &amp; Search Audit, and separately scoped website, search, lead-generation, and care engagements." title="Pricing & Engagements | Anchorline Systems"><section class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Pricing & engagements</p><h1>Know what you're<br />paying for.</h1><p class="lede">Start with a conversation, commission a closer review, or bring us a defined project. We agree on the scope and fee before work begins.</p></section>
<section class="container section"><div class="offer-grid"><article class="offer"><p class="eyebrow">First conversation</p><h2>Growth Review</h2><p class="price">Free</p><ul><li>A brief conversation</li><li>A limited public-site review</li><li>Three initial opportunities</li><li>Supporting observations and a starting point</li></ul><p class="boundary">Qualification-based. No full crawl, competitor report, keyword plan, account access, or implementation instructions.</p><a class="button" href="/growth-review/">Explore the free review <Arrow /></a></article><article class="offer"><p class="eyebrow">Research & recommendations</p><h2>Website & Search Audit</h2><p class="price">$750 <small>one time</small></p><ul><li>One website; five important pages</li><li>Technical and search review</li><li>Two competitor comparisons</li><li>Written priorities and one walkthrough</li></ul><p class="boundary">Research and recommendations. Fixes and implementation are quoted separately. Scope is confirmed before booking.</p><a class="button" href="/website-search-audit/">Explore the paid audit <Arrow /></a></article></div></section>
<section class="service-band"><div class="container section"><p class="eyebrow">Implementation & support</p><h2>A scope that fits the work.</h2><div class="package-grid">{[['Website project','Fixed project fee','Agreed pages, design, development, content responsibilities, search basics, and testing.','website-development'],['Search & content','Defined monthly scope','Agreed technical improvements, useful content, and reporting.','search-visibility'],['Website care','Monthly care agreement','Routine checks and a capped allowance for small changes.','website-care'],['Lead-generation pilot','Scoped pilot','One audience, agreed research and messaging, and a measured test.','lead-generation']].map(([name, model, copy, slug]) => <article><span class="mono">{model}</span><h3>{name}</h3><p>{copy}</p><a class="text-link" href={`/services/${slug}/`}>See the scope <Arrow /></a></article>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="container section faq"><p class="eyebrow">A few practical questions</p><h2>Before we start.</h2><details><summary>Do I have to buy an audit first?</summary><p>No. If your needs are clear enough to quote responsibly, we can go directly to a scoped project.</p></details><details><summary>Is basic SEO an extra charge on a website build?</summary><p>No. Essential metadata, crawlability, mobile usability, and agreed performance testing belong in the build. Ongoing research, content and optimization are separate work.</p></details><details><summary>Are SEO, AEO and GEO separate packages?</summary><p>No. We treat them as related parts of search visibility and explain the specific work included.</p></details><details><summary>Does the audit include fixes?</summary><p>No. The $750 audit provides research, priorities, and a walkthrough. You can use those recommendations with us or another provider.</p></details></section><AuditClose /></Site>
